course: dictionary
lesson: 5726
title: Loot: one word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: One word can have more than one meaning, and the sentence tells you which one. «Pirates sailed away with the loot» means stolen treasure. Here loot is a noun, a thing: the goods that were taken.
explain: Loot can also be a verb, an action word. «Soldiers looted the town» means they stole from the shops and houses. Look at the endings to spot the verb: loot, looted, looting.
explain: In games and parties, loot means something different. «A loot box is a paid mystery prize in a game» means you pay, the box opens, and you find out afterwards what you got. Always check the clues around the word before you decide what it means.
fact: Loot is a noun (a thing) and a verb (an action word).
fact: «Loot» means things stolen, especially by robbers or soldiers, or treasure that is taken.
fact: «Looted» means stole from shops or houses, especially during a war, riot or disaster.
fact: Informal «loot» means things you get, such as presents, sweets or prizes in a game, as in «a loot bag» at a party.
fact: «Jungle» came from Hindi «jangal», wild land, and «loot» came from Hindi «lūṭ», stolen goods.
exercise: «Pirates hid the loot in a cave.» What is the loot? | A ship's sail | A map of the sea | A sleepy parrot | * Stolen treasure
exercise: «Soldiers looted the town.» What does looted mean? | Painted the houses bright colours | Built a new bridge over the river | * Stole from shops and houses in the war
exercise: Ella says «loot boxes» are free surprises. Is she right? | * No, you pay, and you do not know what you will get | No, they are only found in books | Yes, they are always free | Yes, they are given out at school
test: Sam shared the loot from his party bag with his friends. What does loot mean here? | A broken toy | A heavy bag of rubbish | * Sweets and treats | Stolen goods
test: Which word is a verb in «The robbers looted the bank»? | robbers | bank | * looted | the
exam: What does «loot box» mean in «A loot box is a paid mystery prize in a game»? | A box for keeping sweets | * A paid mystery prize in a game | A box that opens by itself | A box of stolen gold
